From: Kevin Liu <11365056+kliu128@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: tell user space when a radio was restarted

After a firmware crash mac80211 restores the interfaces, stations and keys
of a radio, but links that were keyed with the previous firmware instance
pass no traffic: an 802.11s link stays established while every frame is
dropped at the other end, until the peering is done again.

Send a "change" uevent (ATH11K_RECOVERED=1) for the device once its radio
is up again, so that user space can do that.

Signed-off-by: Kevin Liu <11365056+kliu128@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -9281,6 +9281,7 @@
 	struct ath11k_base *ab = ar->ab;
 	int recovery_count;
 	struct ath11k_vif *arvif;
+	bool recovered = false;
 
 	if (reconfig_type != IEEE80211_RECONFIG_TYPE_RESTART)
 		return;
@@ -9292,6 +9293,7 @@
 			    ar->pdev->pdev_id);
 		ar->state = ATH11K_STATE_ON;
 		ieee80211_wake_queues(ar->hw);
+		recovered = true;
 
 		if (ar->ab->hw_params.current_cc_support &&
 		    ar->alpha2[0] != 0 && ar->alpha2[1] != 0)
@@ -9321,6 +9323,18 @@
 	}
 
 	mutex_unlock(&ar->conf_mutex);
+
+	/*
+	 * The interfaces are back, but links that were keyed with the
+	 * previous firmware instance pass no traffic: a mesh link stays
+	 * established and every frame is dropped at the other end. Let user
+	 * space bring them up again.
+	 */
+	if (recovered) {
+		char *envp[] = { "ATH11K_RECOVERED=1", NULL };
+
+		kobject_uevent_env(&ab->dev->kobj, KOBJ_CHANGE, envp);
+	}
 }
 
 static void
